  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor in Morvi?", answer: "Share the programme, subject, level and the exam session your child is preparing for, and a shortlist of tutors who have actually taught that exact course comes back. Since Morvi has no school of its own running the IB, geography plays no part in the match; syllabus knowledge decides who gets shortlisted, and timing gets worked out afterward around your evening. Every match starts with a free trial lesson, and a different tutor is offered if the first one is not a fit." },
    { question: "Do you offer IGCSE home tutors in Morbi for Cambridge and Edexcel?", answer: "Yes, both boards, and the lesson still runs as online private tuition delivered at home rather than a visit to your door. A Cambridge student is matched on syllabus code and tier, Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620 for example, while an Edexcel student is matched on specification and whether they sit Foundation or Higher, with practice drawn from that board's own past papers rather than a mixed bag of both." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Morvi or Morbi?", answer: "No. A tutor calling at a family's door is something IB Gram runs only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR, and Morvi is not covered under either spelling of its name. What runs here instead is genuine online private tuition from home, one-to-one video lessons on a shared screen at a fixed weekly time, with the tutor joining remotely rather than sitting in the living room. It is worth stating plainly so no Morvi family waits for a home visit that will never happen." },
    { question: "Is there an IB or IGCSE school in Morvi (Morbi) itself?", answer: "Not one currently confirmed to teach the IB or a Cambridge or Edexcel IGCSE syllabus. Green Valley International School and Vinay International School both use 'international' in their name but run on CBSE. The Galaxy School in Rajkot, about an hour away, is the nearest confirmed option, holding IB Diploma authorisation and teaching Cambridge IGCSE as well." },
    { question: "What does an IB or IGCSE tutor in Morvi cost?", answer: "It depends on four things: programme, level, subject and session length, and the exact rate for your match is written down before the trial lesson. Diploma HL work usually costs more than MYP or IGCSE Core because fewer tutors have recently taught it. Nobody adds a travel charge, because every lesson is online, and there is no lock-in: you can pause or stop when you like." },
    { question: "Can my child complete the full IB Diploma or IGCSE without attending a local school in Morvi?", answer: "Plenty of Morvi families combine tutoring with an online school, a boarding place in Rajkot or Ahmedabad, or some hybrid of the two, since no Diploma-authorised or Cambridge school currently runs in the city. IB Gram tutors support the academic side of any of these setups but do not handle enrolment or admission at a school; that stays a matter between the family and the institution itself." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial class before I commit?", answer: "Yes, and it is a genuine lesson rather than a sales pitch. A child works through real syllabus content with the tutor over video, nothing charged whether or not the family continues afterward. If things go ahead, the tutor writes up a short plan for the weeks that follow; if the fit is wrong, saying so is enough to trigger another search." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with IB Internal Assessments for a Morvi student?", answer: "Tutors coach the IA but never write any of it. That means helping a student settle on a researchable question, reading the marking criteria line by line, testing whether the data plan will work and commenting frankly on drafts. Writing or rewriting submitted work counts as an academic integrity breach, so it is refused however the request is worded." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you help with for a Morvi student?", answer: "Coverage runs across every major Diploma subject group. In practice, Morvi families most often ask about both Maths routes at HL and SL, the three sciences, Economics, Business Management, English A and Design Technology, plus support with Theory of Knowledge and the Extended Essay, though a request outside that list is always worth raising." },
    { question: "Do you tutor IB MYP and PYP students connected to Morvi, not only the Diploma?", answer: "The full continuum gets covered, not the Diploma alone. MYP requests usually cluster around criterion-based writing in the sciences and Language and Literature, plus the Personal Project's process journal, generally for a child boarding at a school outside Morvi. PYP sessions run shorter and more often, built around reading, number sense and the research skills the Exhibition eventually calls on." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring as effective as in-person tuition for IB or IGCSE students in Morvi?", answer: "Online is the only realistic format here, and for Morvi it is a strong one. No local teacher has in-person IB or IGCSE experience for a visit to compete with, and home visits run only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR anyway. A shared whiteboard, past papers on screen and a saved recording of each worked solution replace most of what a visit offers, while the tutor pool spans the whole country instead of stopping at Rajkot or Ahmedabad." },
    { question: "How are IB Gram tutors verified for Morvi students?", answer: "We check what a tutor holds and has taught recently at the exact level a family needs, and how they handle assessment criteria, before any introduction. With no Morvi school teaching these courses, we look for people who taught that same course elsewhere in India in the last year or two. After the trial lesson, the parent judges the match independently of us." },
    { question: "When should my child in Morvi start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Best at the start of the course: Grade 9 for IGCSE, Class 11 for the Diploma. That gives time to repair foundations before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades pile up together. Starting later still works; lessons then concentrate on the highest-value topics and on timed past papers for the time that is left." },
    { question: "My child is switching from GSEB or CBSE to IB or IGCSE in Morvi. Can a tutor help?", answer: "This comes up constantly here, precisely because no Morvi school teaches either curriculum from the start, so almost every family arrives as a switcher. The usual fix has less to do with subject content and more with exam language: command words like 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' carry specific expectations worth spelling out, alongside a short crash course in planning coursework or an IA, ideally begun the summer before the switch itself happens." },
    { question: "Can sessions happen on weekends or after school hours in Morvi?", answer: "Weekday evenings after school and weekend mornings are what most Morvi families settle on, and both work fine. Business-owning households often prefer a slot starting once the day's factory or trading work has wound down, and around Navratri and Diwali the calendar simply shifts to fit whatever the family has planned. Adding a second slot ahead of mocks is straightforward." },
    { question: "What happens if we are not happy with the tutor in Morvi?", answer: "Tell us and we find you a different tutor. Progress is reviewed every few weeks so a weak fit does not linger, and there is no contract binding a child to someone who is not helping. Pausing or stopping entirely costs nothing extra." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any Morvi school or with the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "No, IB Gram is independent. No school in or near Morvi, and none of the International Baccalaureate, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel, sponsors or represents us. Schools are named here only to show where a curriculum is taught, and tutors follow each school's calendar alongside the board's published syllabus." },
  ],

